/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4520` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation4520` is `x ◇ (y ◇ z) = (x ◇ w) ◇ z`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if a = b then (M.op a a) else if (M.op a b) = b then a else (M.op b a)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_x_y_pxy_y_pxx_x_pyx_Equation4520`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 6 of them below.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
